course: dictionary
lesson: 2970
title: Sound and message: drumbeat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A drumbeat is the sound of a drum being hit, or a steady rhythm made by those sounds. Look at the words around it to find the meaning: «races to a drumbeat» tells you the boats race in time with a drum, so the drum sets the rhythm.
explain: The word can also mean a message that keeps coming back. «A drumbeat of bad news» means bad news arriving again and again, like a steady beat. Ask: is the text about a sound, or about something repeated? The words around the word give the clue.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put "beat of the drum" in place of drumbeat in «races to a drumbeat» and it still makes sense, so you know you are right. Then check the other clues.
fact: A drumbeat is the sound of a drum being hit.
fact: A drumbeat can also be a steady rhythm, like the beat in music.
fact: «A drumbeat of bad news» means bad news that keeps coming again and again.
fact: «The drumbeat of war» means the steady signs that war is getting closer.
fact: In the Dragon Boat Festival, boats race to a drumbeat, so the drum keeps everyone in time.
exercise: «In early summer comes Duānwǔ jié, the Dragon Boat Festival, with races to a drumbeat.» What is a drumbeat here? | A sticky rice parcel | *The beat of a drum that sets the rhythm | A poem about a drowned man | A kind of boat
exercise: Sam says «a drumbeat of bad news» means one drum played very loudly. What does it really mean? | A happy surprise | *Bad news that keeps coming again and again | A drum played very loudly at night | A news channel with a drum in its logo
exercise: Which word in «a steady drumbeat of warnings» tells you the warnings are not stopping? | a | of | *steady | warnings
test: «The drumbeat of war grew louder each year.» What does the drumbeat of war mean? | *The steady signs that war is coming closer | A happy festival with boats | A drum that is broken | A kind of music played at parties
test: Why does the drum matter in a dragon boat race? | It tells the crews to stop and eat | *It keeps the crews moving together in time | It makes the boats float | It lets the crews sleep
exam: Maya reads «a drumbeat of bad news» and says it means a real drum. What is the best answer? | Maya is right, because drumbeat only ever means a sound | *Maya is wrong, because the words around it show bad news that keeps coming | Maya is right, because a drum must be in the news | Maya is wrong, because drums cannot make sounds
